# A Guided Laboratory for Zero-Knowledge Identification

A prover claims to know a preimage $w$ of a public target $y$ under a homomorphism $\varphi$. The central achievement is a three-way balance: honest conversations always pass, one conversation can be simulated without the witness, and two opposite answers under one commitment expose a witness.

